</div></div>
</div></section><section class="ch" id="decisions"><div class="shell">
 <div class="ch-txt head"><p class="lab">Decisions</p><h2 class="claim">How we made it work.</h2></div>
 <div class="decs">
 <article class="dec cms"><div class="dec-txt"><span class="dn">01</span><h3>One home page, with each section tagged by vertical.</h3>
  <p>We already had a CMS. With engineering, product and the content team, we looked at a few ways to show different home pages. The one everyone agreed on: tag each section of the page with the verticals that should see it.</p>
  <p>The content team keeps one page, and a new vertical needs no new build. We started with Grocery and IR, and the team can add any category next.</p></div>
  <div class="dec-m"><figure class="cms-shot">
   <div class="cms-win"><div class="cms-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>strapi.tradeling.com</span></div><img src="/work/tradeling/i/strapi-content-manager.jpg" alt="The home page in Strapi's Content Manager: a list of sections, with the Activity Panel open, shown to guests and retailers, and to guests and restaurants." width="932" height="604" decoding="async"></div>
   <div class="cms-card"><img src="/work/tradeling/i/strapi-banner-ad.jpg" alt="A banner ad section in Strapi, tagged with the user segments that see it: guest, individual and retailer, then guest." width="1522" height="1060" decoding="async"></div>
  </figure></div></article>
 <article class="dec shv"><div class="dec-txt"><span class="dn">02</span><h3>Shelves built from what each business buys.</h3>
  <p>Tradeling's catalogue follows its internal structure, not the way a buyer thinks. With the data analyst, I looked at what each type of business actually buys, then built new shelves on top of the catalogue for each vertical, Grocery and IR: renamed some, merged others, and pulled a few in from other categories. Here is the grocery store.</p>
</div>
  <div class="dec-m"><div class="opts-box"><div class="bhead"><span></span><span>In Tradeling’s catalogue</span><span></span><span>On a grocery store’s home</span></div><div class="brows"><div class="brow"><p class="mv-l">Rename</p><div class="b-src"><span class="part"><b>Grains &amp; Pulses</b><em>Food &amp; Beverages</em></span></div><span class="b-br" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="b-out"><span class="res">Rice, Pasta &amp; Pulses</span><p class="mc-n">Named the way grocery stores ask for it.</p></div></div><div class="brow"><p class="mv-l">Merge</p><div class="b-src"><span class="part"><b>Oils &amp; Fats</b><em>Pantry</em></span><span class="part"><b>Baking Ingredients</b><em>Pantry</em></span><span class="part"><b>Baking Decorations</b><em>Pantry</em></span><span class="part"><b>Sugar</b><em>Pantry</em></span><span class="part"><b>Stock</b><em>Pantry</em></span></div><span class="b-br" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="b-out"><span class="res">Cooking &amp; Baking</span><p class="mc-n">Five shelves a grocery store thinks of as one.</p></div></div><div class="brow"><p class="mv-l">Pull across</p><div class="b-src"><span class="part"><b>Batteries</b><em>Office &amp; Stationery</em></span><span class="part"><b>Small Kitchen Appliances</b><em>Home &amp; Garden</em></span><span class="part"><b>Accessories</b><em>Consumer Electronics</em></span></div><span class="b-br" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="b-out"><span class="res">Electronics</span><p class="mc-n">Only the electronics a grocery store sells. No large appliances.</p></div></div></div></div></div></article>
 </div>
</div></section><section class="ch" id="features"><div class="shell">
 <div class="ch-txt head"><p class="lab">Features with impact</p><h2 class="claim">Three features that changed how customers use the app.</h2></div>
 <div class="decs">
 <article class="dec negv"><div class="dec-txt"><span class="dn">01</span><h3>Negotiation, inside the app.</h3><p>Customers trusted agents because they could ask for a better price. So we put that in the app: ask for a price, get a counter offer, accept.</p><p>The price never goes below the floor without approval from the back office. An accepted price is held for a limited time, shorter for fast-selling products.</p><div class="stat"><b>+60%</b><span>increase in orders negotiated in the app, instead of through agents</span></div></div><div class="dec-m"><div class="nx-stage"><div class="nx-phone" data-img="/work/tradeling/i/bd917dfdb139.jpg" role="img" aria-label="Negotiation in the app: the buyer asks for 10 units at 4,500, the seller counters at 4,900, the buyer counters at 4,600.80, the seller accepts and the deal is added to the cart"></div></div></div></article>
 <article class="dec "><div class="dec-txt"><span class="dn">02</span><h3>Orders and payments due, first thing on the home page.</h3><p>Shop owners are busy and do not browse. Order status and payments due used to be several taps deep. The activity panel shows them at the top of the home page.</p><p>Customers started opening the app just to check on their orders, and that became a habit. Sessions got longer, and calls to customer support about orders went down.</p><div class="stat"><b>15%</b><span>click-through on the activity panel</span></div></div><div class="dec-m"><div class="av" data-icons="{&quot;chevup&quot;: &quot;&lt;svg viewBox=\&quot;0 0 20 20\&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=\&quot;evenodd\&quot; clip-rule=\&quot;evenodd\&quot; d=\&quot;M9.26343 6.76343C9.67023 6.35663 10.3298 6.35663 10.7366 6.76343L15.7366 11.7634C16.1434 12.1702 16.1434 12.8298 15.7366 13.2366C15.3298 13.6434 14.6702 13.6434 14.2634 13.2366L10 8.97314L5.73657 13.2366C5.32977 13.6434 4.67023 13.6434 4.26343 13.2366C3.85663 12.8298 3.85663 12.1702 4.26343 11.7634L9.26343 6.76343Z\&quot; fill=\&quot;#0B0C0D\&quot;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&quot;, &quot;chevr&quot;: &quot;&lt;svg viewBox=\&quot;0 0 20 20\&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=\&quot;evenodd\&quot; clip-rule=\&quot;evenodd\&quot; d=\&quot;M6.76343 4.26343C7.17023 3.85663 7.82977 3.85663 8.23657 4.26343L13.2366 9.26343C13.6434 9.67023 13.6434 10.3298 13.2366 10.7366L8.23657 15.7366C7.82977 16.1434 7.17023 16.1434 6.76343 15.7366C6.35663 15.3298 6.35663 14.6702 6.76343 14.2634L11.0269 10L6.76343 5.73657C6.35663 5.32977 6.35663 4.67023 6.76343 4.26343Z\&quot; fill=\&quot;#0B0C0D\&quot;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&quot;, &quot;file&quot;: &quot;&lt;svg viewBox=\&quot;0 0 20 20\&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=\&quot;evenodd\&quot; clip-rule=\&quot;evenodd\&quot; d=\&quot;M10.625 2.71371C10.4875 2.70958 10.2953 2.70833 10.0098 2.70833H7.33333C6.61608 2.70833 6.14079 2.70914 5.77616 2.73893C5.4237 2.76773 5.26733 2.81833 5.17126 2.86728C4.89686 3.0071 4.67376 3.230